{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Zip","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Module.Basic"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossingRule.pn_product_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossingRule.pn_product_formula","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L316-L316","doc":"The chirality factor factorises as a product over pn crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossingRule.q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossingRule.q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L314-L314","doc":"`q > 0` (substrate regime). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossingRule.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossingRule.mk","kind":"ctor","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L312-L312","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossingRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossingRule","kind":"class","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L295-L321","doc":"**Empirical multiplicative crossing rule (conjecture).**\n\nFor nuclear knots (`D`, `T`, `³He`, `⁴He`), paper assigns\n\n  `a_K = Π_{c ∈ pn-crossings(β)} (1 + sign(c)·h)`.\n\nThis rule reproduces all three paper assignments:\n- `D` (1 positive crossing): `a_D = 1 + h`.\n- `T`, `³He` (1 positive + 1 negative): `a = 1 - h²`.\n- `⁴He` (2 positive + 2 negative): `a = (1 - h²)²`.\n\nA categorical derivation of **why** each pn crossing contributes\n`(1 ± h)` requires specifying the pn coupling in Schur–Weyl terms\nand is left open. The most structurally natural origin is the\nspin-½ braiding eigenvalue of `U_q(𝔰𝔩₂)` on the symmetric\ncomponent of `V₁ ⊗ V₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossing.sign_pm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossing.sign_pm","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L293-L293","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossing.sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossing.sign","kind":"def","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L292-L292","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossing.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossing.mk","kind":"ctor","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L291-L291","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.PNCrossing","kind":"structure","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L290-L293","doc":"A signed inter-nucleon (pn) crossing with sign ±1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.chirality_writhe_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.chirality_writhe_zero","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L267-L286","doc":"**Corollary: amphichiral knots have vanishing first-order chirality.**\n\nWhen writhe `w = 0`, the linearisation gives `a_K = 1 + O(h²)`.\nThe chirality correction is second-order, consistent with\n`a_{4_1} = 1 - h²` for the amphichiral figure-eight knot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.chirality_writhe_ribbon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.chirality_writhe_ribbon","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L178-L263","doc":"**Main proposition — writhe-linearisation of the chirality factor.**\n\nLet `β ∈ B_n` be a braid with writhe `w = w(β)`.  Let\n`h = q - q⁻¹` be the Hecke deformation.  Let\n`⟨c⟩_β = Σ_λ w_λ χ^λ(β) κ_λ / Σ_λ w_λ χ^λ(β)` be the\ncharacter-weighted average Jucys–Murphy content.  Then\n\n  `a_K(β) = 1 + w · h · ⟨c⟩_β + O(h²)`,\n\nand the first-order coefficient `c_avg` is **exactly** `⟨c⟩_β`\n(not the vacuous 0): the chirality factor is **linear in `h`** and\n**linear in the writhe** to first order. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:chirality-writhe-ribbon-derivation","label":"prop:chirality-writhe-ribbon-derivation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-writhe-ribbon-derivation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.log_q_first_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.log_q_first_order","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L123-L153","doc":"**Logarithm identity at first order in `h`.**\nFor `q > 0` with deformation parameter `h = q - q⁻¹`,\n`ln q = h/2 + O(h³)`.  Equivalently, `q^{2κ} = 1 + κ·h + O(h²)`.\n\nThis is the key analytic input for the linearisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.chiralityFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.chiralityFactor","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L100-L119","doc":"The **chirality factor** for a braid `β` with writhe `w` is the\nratio of the ribbon-twisted Markov trace to the untwisted trace:\n\n  `a_K(β) = (Σ_λ w_λ χ^λ(β) q^{w·κ_λ}) / (Σ_λ w_λ χ^λ(β))`.\n\nWe record this as a real number; positivity in the physical regime\nis not formalized here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.RibbonTwistEigenvalue.framing_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.RibbonTwistEigenvalue.framing_formula","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L94-L94","doc":"The eigenvalue formula: `θ_n^{w}|_{V_λ} = q^{2w·κ_λ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.RibbonTwistEigenvalue.framing_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.RibbonTwistEigenvalue.framing_eigenvalue","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L92-L92","doc":"The eigenvalue of `θ_n^{w}` on `V_λ` is `q^{2w·κ_λ}` (Kauffman framing:\nthe ribbon twist acts as `q^{2κ_λ}`, so a writhe-`w` framing change\nmultiplies channel `λ` by `q^{2w·κ_λ}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.RibbonTwistEigenvalue.q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.RibbonTwistEigenvalue.q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L88-L88","doc":"`q > 0` (substrate regime). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.RibbonTwistEigenvalue.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.RibbonTwistEigenvalue.mk","kind":"ctor","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.RibbonTwistEigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.RibbonTwistEigenvalue","kind":"class","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L79-L96","doc":"**Ribbon twist eigenvalue.**\nThe full-twist central element `θ_n ∈ Z(H_n(q))` acts on the\nirreducible Hecke module `V_λ` by the scalar `q^{2κ_λ}`.\nWe expose this as an axiom class; it is a standard consequence of\nthe Jones–Ocneanu ribbon structure on `H_n(q)`.\n\nRef: [kassel1995] Ch. XIV; [mathas1999] §3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.HeckeCharValue.val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.HeckeCharValue.val","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The character value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.HeckeCharValue.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.HeckeCharValue.mk","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.HeckeCharValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.HeckeCharValue","kind":"structure","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L71-L75","doc":"The Hecke character evaluated at the braid `β` in channel `λ`:\n`χ^λ(β) ∈ ℝ` (a real specialization of the character polynomial). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.WedderburnChannel.weight_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.WedderburnChannel.weight_pos","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Weights are positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.WedderburnChannel.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.WedderburnChannel.weight","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Plancherel weight `w_λ = dim_q(λ)² / [n]_q!` (positive real). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.WedderburnChannel.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.WedderburnChannel.kappa","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Total Jucys–Murphy content `κ_λ := Σ_{x ∈ λ} (col x - row x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.WedderburnChannel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.WedderburnChannel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.WedderburnChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ChiralityWritheRibbon.WedderburnChannel","kind":"structure","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ChiralityWritheRibbon.lean#L58-L69","doc":"A Wedderburn channel is a partition `λ ⊢ n`, encoded here by\nits total Jucys–Murphy content `κ_λ = Σ c(x)` and its\nquantum dimension (Plancherel weight denominator).  We keep the\nabstract structure parameter-free so that the ribbon computation\nis independent of the underlying Young combinatorics module. ","signatureChunk":0}]}